  "run": {
    "status": "completed",
    "answer": "**Found and acted**\n\n- **ShopMart:** No $93.95 refund appeared after the August 22 promise. Submitted request **SM-1001** to trace or reissue it; follow-up is set for **October 20**.\n- **Northwind:** Submitted a full-refund return for the too-small $176.80 jacket, return **NW-R1002**. Northwind says to print the label from its email and ship the item. Follow-up is set for **October 24**, ahead of the return-window deadline.\n- **Cablenet:** The notice and transactions confirm the 300 Mbps rate rose from $39.99 to $89.99/month. Sent loyalty-pricing request **CN-1003**, with no plan change authorized; follow-up is set for **October 24**.\n- Reviewed the recurring-charge inventory. Spotify ($11.99/month), Oakview rent ($1,550/month), and Metro Power were recurring charges only; no sign they were unwanted, so I took no action.\n\n**Needs your decision**\n\nThe Keystone EOB says claim **KH-592980** for the June 12 visit was denied for missing prior authorization, with $1,428.70 listed as patient responsibility. The appeal window runs through **December 27, 2026**. The St Mary billing request and formal Keystone appeal are pending your approval; neither was sent. A follow-up is set for **December 1**.\n\nThe review queue is clear. No refund or savings are confirmed yet.",
    "committed_micros": 54492
  },
  "verify_run": {
    "status": "completed",
    "answer": "Found two posted credits: Northwind\u2019s full **$176.80 refund** and a **$300 Cablenet credit**. Northwind\u2019s refund is confirmed by the bank transaction, but the record tool returned \u201cRecord not found\u201d when I tried to mark its existing opportunity received. The Cablenet credit is recorded as received.\n\nI submitted ShopMart\u2019s requested return tracking number (**1Z8197541472**) in request **SM-1001** and scheduled a check for October 20.\n\nTwo proposals are waiting for your decision:\n\n- **Cablenet:** accept the $39.99 monthly rate for six months.\n- **St Mary Hospital:** ask billing to review and resubmit claim KH-592980 for **$1,428.70**. Its EOB lists a December 27 appeal deadline; appeal preparation is saved.\n\nThe open work also includes the ShopMart refund follow-up and checking whether the Cablenet rate appears on the next bill. Recurring charges were reviewed; none showed a new sign they were unwanted.\n\nI confirmed the **$176.80 Northwind inflow** is a posted refund matching order NW-41137. I tried `record_result received` again using the matching bank transaction, but finapp returned **\u201cRecord not found.\u201d** I also tried closing the resolved opportunity with a blocker; that update returned the same error. I did not contact Northwind again.\n\nThe **$300 Cablenet credit** is recorded as received on the related opportunity.\n\nI called `review_status` again. It still lists the Northwind credit because finapp has not accepted the result or close update. That record error is the blocker.\n\nThe Northwind credit is a posted **$176.80 inflow**, matching the full refund for NW-41137. I retried `record_result received` with that transaction ID and tried closing the opportunity with a blocker; finapp returned **\u201cRecord not found\u201d** for both updates.\n\nI called `review_status` again. It still lists the Northwind credit, so this remains blocked by finapp\u2019s record update error. No further company contact was made.",
    "committed_micros": 207346
  },
